+## Automatic security gate
+
+In an OpenCode `goal` or `auto` session, the plugin watches `edit`, `write`,
+and `patch` results. After a code edit it waits 2.5s, hashes the current
+workspace diff, and runs one bounded OCR review for that hash:
+
+- `--effort low`; `medium` when the diff is >200 changed lines or touches
+  auth/crypto/input/secret paths;
+- `--max-tokens-budget 40000`, `--timeout 2`, `--concurrency 4`;
+- keeps only `category security|bug` and `severity critical|high`;
+- injects a compact `[security-gate]` system note on the next request.
+
+The model is an invariant: `--provider deepseek --model deepseek-flash`, the
+same model as the OpenCode agent. The gate changes effort/scope, never the
+model. Override only when the OpenCode model changes with
+`OCR_GATE_PROVIDER` / `OCR_GATE_MODEL`.
+
+Stop rules: 3 runs per session, 120k total tokens, 2 empty runs, 2 injections,
+2 OCR errors, or an unchanged diff hash. Disable with
+`OPENCODE_SECURITY_GATE=0` or `OCR_SECURITY_GATE=0`. The full policy lives in
+the OCR `code-audit` skill; `/audit` is the manual/final path.
+
 ## Behavior and safety
 
 - Reviews use `--audience agent` and JSON output.
